Frame validation is now explicit: nonzero dimensions up to 4096 per axis, checked packed-byte sizing capped at 64 MiB, and a finite backing scale in `(0, 16]`. For presentation I’m using copied `CFData` as the image provider, so the frame’s input buffer can be released after the synchronous call while Core Graphics retains the image data. The layer’s `contents` property is the single publication point.
