index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..d3bc0e08fa7f1c0ab7f2ab7de55a85167845d40c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/rust/crates/vexel-platform-apple/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+# vexel-platform-apple
+
+This crate owns the macOS native window and event boundary. `RgbaFrame` and
+`Window::present_rgba` form a pixel presentation seam for owned top-left,
+tightly packed RGBA8 data in sRGB with premultiplied alpha. Frame dimensions
+are limited to 4096 by 4096 (64 MiB), and backing scale must be finite and in
+`(0, 16]`.
+
+Presentation copies frame bytes into Core Foundation data, prepares a
+CoreGraphics image, then assigns that retained image to the native view's
+Core Animation layer. The layer owns its current image; replacement is a
+synchronous single-property publication, with the prior image retained by the
+layer until replacement. This is only the frame presentation seam. It does
+not integrate a document model, editor workflow, SVG renderer, or complete V1
+application flow. Package tests do not establish live AppKit rendering on a
+macOS GUI session.
